From d0d429a2420143f4aa970de5ed8e5001eaf3dd2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:06:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Update the upstream signing key

Update p11-kit-release-keyring.gpg to the current copy at
https://p11-glue.github.io/p11-glue/p11-kit/p11-kit-release-keyring.gpg,
the URL the spec names for it (same certificate(s)).
p11-kit-release-keyring.gpg was in the lookaside cache, which a pull
request cannot update, so it moves into git (dropped from sources).

The current key is needed to verify the release signature with
openpgpverify (sqv), which checks that the key was valid when the
release was signed.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 .gitignore                  |   1 -
 p11-kit-release-keyring.gpg | Bin 0 -> 13085 bytes
 sources                     |   1 -
 3 files changed, 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 p11-kit-release-keyring.gpg

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index 75da23a..0ece024 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -37,7 +37,6 @@
